EXPERIMENT - 3 (LEETCODE Problem 232)

Aim - Implement a first in first out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

Algorithm - Implement Queue Using Two Stacks

            Step 1: Create two stacks, Stack1 and Stack2.

            Step 2: To insert (Push) an element:
            a) Move all elements from Stack1 to Stack2.
            b) Push the new element into Stack1.
            c) Move all elements back from Stack2 to Stack1.

            Step 3: To delete (Pop) an element:
            a) If Stack1 is empty, display "Queue Underflow".
            b) Otherwise, pop and return the top element of Stack1.\

            Step 4: To view the front element (Peek):
            a) If Stack1 is empty, display "Queue is Empty".
            b) Otherwise, return the top element of Stack1.

            Step 5: To check whether the queue is empty:
            a) If Stack1 is empty, return True.
            b) Otherwise, return False.

            Step 6: Stop.

Code -  #include <stack>
        using namespace std;

        class MyQueue {
        public:
        stack<int> s1, s2;

        MyQueue() {

        }

        void push(int x) {
        while (!s1.empty()) {
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }

        s1.push(x);

        while (!s2.empty()) {
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
        }

        int pop() {
        int x = s1.top();
        s1.pop();
       return x;
       }

       int peek() {
        return s1.top();
       }

       bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
       }
       };
